{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00116",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.85,
      "end_seconds": 5.93,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "Doctor, this one's ready for you. Everything's on the chart, but I'll go through it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.25,
      "end_seconds": 11.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "Okay, thank you. Good morning, tell me what's been going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 12.96,
      "end_seconds": 19.14,
      "duration_seconds": 6.18,
      "text": "Doctor, uh, I've come along because I know the history, if it helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.61,
      "end_seconds": 23.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. We'll go through it together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.05,
      "end_seconds": 29.94,
      "duration_seconds": 5.89,
      "text": "Mainly aching in my thighs. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.51,
      "end_seconds": 34.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "And when did that start? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.73,
      "end_seconds": 45.24,
      "duration_seconds": 9.51,
      "text": "It's been four weeks, I'm fairly sure. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.96,
      "end_seconds": 49.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Okay, on a normal day, how strong is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.77,
      "end_seconds": 57.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.47,
      "text": "Well, it's... hard to say, it's kind of... I don't know—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.86,
      "end_seconds": 62.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "Take your time. Mild, moderate, or severe, if you had to pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.0,
      "end_seconds": 64.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "It's moderate, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.36,
      "end_seconds": 68.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Does anything bring it on or make it worse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.67,
      "end_seconds": 71.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Yes, climbing stairs. That makes it worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.03,
      "end_seconds": 75.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.57,
      "end_seconds": 80.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get tiredness as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.54,
      "end_seconds": 87.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.57,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 87.21,
      "end_seconds": 92.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.24,
      "text": "Uh, tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.33,
      "end_seconds": 95.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.84,
      "end_seconds": 102.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "That's fine, one at a time. I'll ask about everything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.87,
      "end_seconds": 105.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "The tiredness? That's been for ten days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.5,
      "end_seconds": 108.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Has there been cramps too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.4,
      "end_seconds": 110.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Yes, I have."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.55,
      "end_seconds": 118.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "Have you had aching in your thighs before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.3,
      "end_seconds": 124.66,
      "duration_seconds": 5.36,
      "text": "Yes, something like this happened last winter, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.02,
      "end_seconds": 130.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any recent heavy exercise, trouble swallowing or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.28,
      "end_seconds": 142.59,
      "duration_seconds": 11.31,
      "text": "No, no recent heavy exercise, no trouble swallowing, no fever. I did have weakness getting out of a chair at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.21,
      "end_seconds": 145.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "Any rash, joint swelling or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.72,
      "end_seconds": 148.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "No. None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.67,
      "end_seconds": 151.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.5,
      "end_seconds": 153.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "Nothing there, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.17,
      "end_seconds": 158.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.38,
      "end_seconds": 160.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.31,
      "end_seconds": 166.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.54,
      "end_seconds": 179.94,
      "duration_seconds": 12.4,
      "text": "Yes, high blood pressure. I have an underactive thyroid, for five years. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it. I've had high cholesterol for about a year now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.89,
      "end_seconds": 185.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.51,
      "end_seconds": 194.56,
      "duration_seconds": 8.05,
      "text": "I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.24,
      "end_seconds": 199.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.67,
      "end_seconds": 204.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "I had my tonsils out when I was a child."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.85,
      "end_seconds": 208.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "Has anything about your daily routine changed lately?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.36,
      "end_seconds": 225.86,
      "duration_seconds": 16.5,
      "text": "Not really, the days are pretty much the same, work and home, and I've been trying to fit appointments in around my schedule, which isn't always easy, so I'm glad we could find a time today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.18,
      "end_seconds": 227.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Right, do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.07,
      "end_seconds": 232.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "I have a couple of drinks on the weekend."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.86,
      "end_seconds": 236.56,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.62,
      "end_seconds": 240.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "No, I don't smoke and never have."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.48,
      "end_seconds": 245.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 246.0,
      "end_seconds": 249.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Amlodipine. I take it 5 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.48,
      "end_seconds": 252.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.49,
      "end_seconds": 258.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "About six months. I'm on Thyronorm, 50 micrograms, every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 258.49,
      "end_seconds": 266.94,
      "duration_seconds": 8.45,
      "text": "Doctor, you know, I think the last prescription for the Thyronorm was 25 micrograms. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.45,
      "end_seconds": 270.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "I see. Is the most recent prescription on you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.21,
      "end_seconds": 282.14,
      "duration_seconds": 10.93,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. Rosuvastatin, 10 milligrams, at night for my cholesterol. I'd been on ramipril, not any more though, I stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.77,
      "end_seconds": 285.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "I want to open your previous notes quickly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 286.04,
      "end_seconds": 286.91,
      "duration_seconds": 0.87,
      "text": "Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.79,
      "end_seconds": 302.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Does anything run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.65,
      "end_seconds": 305.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "My uncle had colon cancer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 306.5,
      "end_seconds": 318.98,
      "duration_seconds": 12.48,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Blood pressure 119 over 78, respiratory rate 15, weight 95 kilos. Pulse is 68 beats a minute, saturation 98 percent, temperature 36.7, height 159 centimetres."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.98,
      "end_seconds": 336.44,
      "duration_seconds": 14.46,
      "text": "Good, thank you. Just so you know how the rest of the visit will go: I'll finish my notes, we'll agree on the plan, and the front desk will help with anything that needs booking. You shouldn't need to chase anything yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 336.9,
      "end_seconds": 340.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Good, I was wondering how this would go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.42,
      "end_seconds": 358.9,
      "duration_seconds": 18.48,
      "text": "Putting together what you've described, my working impression is muscle symptoms that may be related to the cholesterol tablet. The reason I say that is that the way you describe it fits together. I can't rule out an underactive thyroid yet. I can't rule out a vitamin D deficiency yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 359.32,
      "end_seconds": 361.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Is it something serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.33,
      "end_seconds": 380.61,
      "duration_seconds": 18.28,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's muscle symptoms that may be related to the cholesterol tablet, and we'll know more once the a vitamin D level is back. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had aching in your thighs for four weeks, moderate, and no rash or recent heavy exercise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 381.13,
      "end_seconds": 383.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 384.28,
      "end_seconds": 411.32,
      "duration_seconds": 27.04,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a vitamin D level for muscle weakness. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. Let's get a creatine kinase level, for muscle pain. Let's get a thyroid test, for muscle weakness. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. Don't stop any of your tablets on your own, we'll decide after the blood test."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 412.67,
      "end_seconds": 431.54,
      "duration_seconds": 18.87,
      "text": "Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 432.44,
      "end_seconds": 433.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 434.59,
      "end_seconds": 442.85,
      "duration_seconds": 8.26,
      "text": "I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if the symptoms get worse. Come back in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 443.5,
      "end_seconds": 447.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 448.29,
      "end_seconds": 452.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "Okay, summarise it for me, what's the plan from your side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 452.76,
      "end_seconds": 456.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "So, I come back in two weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0070",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 457.19,
      "end_seconds": 460.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Okay, yes, exactly right. Good. Look after yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0071",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 460.95,
      "end_seconds": 462.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "I appreciate your time, doctor."
    }
  ]
}